"To simplify the expression \\((5-3i)(-4+3i)\\), we will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials):\n\n\\begin{align*}\n(5-3i)(-4+3i) &= 5(-4) + 5(3i) - 3i(-4) + 3i(3i) \\\\\n&= -20 + 15i + 12i + 9i^2 \\\\\n&= -20 + 15i + 12i - 9(-1) \\quad \\text{(since } i^2 = -1 \\text{)} \\\\\n&= -20 + 15i + 12i + 9 \\\\\n&= -11 + 27i.\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, the simplified form of the expression is \\(\\boxed{-11 + 27i}\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(-11 + 27i\\). I hope it is correct."
