"First, we need to rewrite the quadratic equation in standard form:\n\n\\[ x^2 - 4x - 14 = 3x + 16 \\]\n\nMove all terms to one side:\n\n\\[ x^2 - 4x - 14 - 3x - 16 = 0 \\]\n\n\\[ x^2 - 7x - 30 = 0 \\]\n\nNext, we factor the quadratic equation:\n\n\\[ (x - 10)(x + 3) = 0 \\]\n\nSet each factor equal to zero to find the solutions:\n\n\\[ x - 10 = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x + 3 = 0 \\]\n\n\\[ x = 10 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = -3 \\]\n\nThe solutions are \\( x = 10 \\) and \\( x = -3 \\). The positive difference between these solutions is:\n\n\\[ |10 - (-3)| = |10 + 3| = 13 \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{13}\\)."
