"To factor the expression \\(28z^{97} + 7z^{96}\\), we first identify the greatest common factor (GCF) of the terms. The GCF of the coefficients 28 and 7 is 7, and the GCF of the variables \\(z^{97}\\) and \\(z^{96}\\) is \\(z^{96}\\). Therefore, the GCF of the entire expression is \\(7z^{96}\\).\n\nWe can factor out the GCF from each term in the expression:\n\n\\[\n28z^{97} + 7z^{96} = 7z^{96}(4z + 1)\n\\]\n\nThus, the factored form of the expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7z^{96}(4z + 1)}\n\\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(7z^{96}(4z + 1)\\). I hope it is correct."
