"To find the coordinates of point \\( A \\), we need to solve the system of equations given by the lines \\( 3y = x \\) and \\( 2x + 5y = 11 \\).\n\nFirst, substitute \\( x = 3y \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ 2(3y) + 5y = 11 \\]\n\\[ 6y + 5y = 11 \\]\n\\[ 11y = 11 \\]\n\\[ y = 1 \\]\n\nNow, substitute \\( y = 1 \\) back into the first equation to find \\( x \\):\n\\[ 3y = x \\]\n\\[ 3(1) = x \\]\n\\[ x = 3 \\]\n\nThus, the coordinates of point \\( A \\) are \\( (3, 1) \\).\n\nThe sum of the coordinates of point \\( A \\) is:\n\\[ 3 + 1 = 4 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the coordinates of point \\( A \\) is \\( \\boxed{4} \\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\( 4 \\). I hope it is correct."
