"To solve the equation \\(\\sqrt[3]{x\\sqrt{x}} = 7\\), we start by raising both sides to the power of 3 to eliminate the cube root:\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\sqrt[3]{x\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^3 = 7^3\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\nx\\sqrt{x} = 343\n\\]\n\nNext, we square both sides to eliminate the square root:\n\n\\[\n(x\\sqrt{x})^2 = 343^2\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\nx^3 = 117647\n\\]\n\nTo find \\(x\\), we take the cube root of both sides:\n\n\\[\nx = \\sqrt[3]{117647}\n\\]\n\nWe know that:\n\n\\[\n117647 = 27^3\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{117647} = 27\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(x\\) is 27. The final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{27}\n\\]"
