"To find the sum of the odd integers between 46 and 64, we first identify the sequence of odd integers in this range. The first odd integer after 46 is 47, and the last odd integer before 64 is 63. The sequence of odd integers between 46 and 64 is:\n\n\\[ 47, 49, 51, 53, 55, 57, 59, 61, 63 \\]\n\nThere are 9 terms in this sequence. The sum of the first \\( n \\) odd integers is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ S_n = n^2 \\]\n\nHere, \\( n = 9 \\), so the sum of the first 9 odd integers is:\n\n\\[ S_9 = 9^2 \\]\n\nCalculating this, we get:\n\n\\[ 9^2 = 81 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the odd integers between 46 and 64 is \\( \\boxed{81} \\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $81$. I hope it is correct."
