"The binomial coefficient $\\dbinom{22}{19}$ is defined as $\\frac{22!}{19! \\cdot 3!}$. We can simplify this by canceling out the common terms in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\dbinom{22}{19} &= \\frac{22!}{19! \\cdot 3!} \\\\\n&= \\frac{22 \\cdot 21 \\cdot 20 \\cdot 19!}{19! \\cdot 3!} \\\\\n&= \\frac{22 \\cdot 21 \\cdot 20}{3!} \\\\\n&= \\frac{22 \\cdot 21 \\cdot 20}{3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{22 \\cdot 21 \\cdot 20}{6} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9240}{6} \\\\\n&= \\boxed{1540}.\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, $\\dbinom{22}{19} = \\boxed{1540}$.\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $1540$."
