"Given that the roots of the polynomial \\( f(x) = x^4 + ax^2 + bx + c \\) are \\( 2 \\), \\( -3 \\), and \\( 5 \\), we can express the polynomial in factored form as:\n\n\\[ f(x) = (x - 2)(x + 3)(x - 5) \\]\n\nFirst, we expand this product:\n\n\\[ f(x) = (x - 2)(x + 3)(x - 5) \\]\n\\[ f(x) = (x^2 - 6)(x - 5) \\]\n\\[ f(x) = x^3 - 5x^2 - 6x + 30 \\]\n\nFrom this, we can identify the coefficients:\n- \\( a = -5 \\)\n- \\( b = -6 \\)\n- \\( c = 30 \\)\n\nNow, we need to find \\( a + b + c \\):\n\n\\[ a + b + c = -5 - 6 + 30 = 19 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( a + b + c \\) is \\(\\boxed{19}\\)."
