"We can use the AM-GM inequality to find the minimum value of the given expression.\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the expression as:\n\\[\\frac{a}{b + c + d} + \\frac{b}{a + c + d} + \\frac{c}{a + b + d} + \\frac{d}{a + b + c}.\\]\n\nBy the AM-GM inequality, we have:\n\\[\\frac{a}{b + c + d} \\geq \\frac{1}{4},\\]\n\\[\\frac{b}{a + c + d} \\geq \\frac{1}{4},\\]\n\\[\\frac{c}{a + b + d} \\geq \\frac{1}{4},\\]\n\\[\\frac{d}{a + b + c} \\geq \\frac{1}{4}.\\]\n\nAdding these inequalities, we get:\n\\[\\frac{a}{b + c + d} + \\frac{b}{a + c + d} + \\frac{c}{a + b + d} + \\frac{d}{a + b + c} \\geq \\frac{1}{2}.\\]\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of the given expression is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)."
