"Let's denote the initial value of the stock as \\( V \\).\n\nOn Monday, the stock loses 10% of its value. Therefore, the value of the stock at the end of Monday is:\n\\[ V - 0.1V = 0.9V \\]\n\nOn Tuesday, the stock loses 20% of the value it had at the end of Monday. Therefore, the value of the stock at the end of Tuesday is:\n\\[ 0.9V - 0.2 \\times 0.9V = 0.9V - 0.18V = 0.72V \\]\n\nThe overall percent loss in value from the beginning of Monday to the end of Tuesday is the difference between the initial value and the final value:\n\\[ V - 0.72V = 0.28V \\]\n\nTo find the percent loss, we divide the loss by the initial value and multiply by 100:\n\\[ \\frac{0.28V}{V} \\times 100 = 28\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the overall percent loss is \\(\\boxed{28}\\)."
