"To find the measure of the fourth angle in a quadrilateral, we can use the fact that the sum of the interior angles in any quadrilateral is \\(360^\\circ\\).\n\nGiven:\n- One angle is \\(21^\\circ\\),\n- Another is \\(66^\\circ\\),\n- The third is \\(134^\\circ\\).\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of these three angles:\n\\[\n21^\\circ + 66^\\circ + 134^\\circ = 221^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNext, we subtract this sum from \\(360^\\circ\\) to find the measure of the fourth angle:\n\\[\n360^\\circ - 221^\\circ = 139^\\circ\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of the fourth angle is \\(\\boxed{139^\\circ}\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(139^\\circ\\). I hope it is correct."
