"First, we need to determine the number of cards that are either odd numbers or spades. There are 4 odd numbers (3, 5, 7, 9) in a standard deck, and each number has 4 cards (one for each suit). Therefore, there are \\(4 \\times 4 = 16\\) odd number cards.\n\nNext, there are 13 spades in a standard deck.\n\nHowever, we must be careful not to double-count the cards that are both odd numbers and spades. There are 4 odd number spades (one for each odd number).\n\nUsing the principle of inclusion-exclusion, we calculate the total number of cards that are either odd numbers or spades:\n\\[\n16 + 13 - 4 = 25\n\\]\n\nThe total number of cards in the deck is 52. Therefore, the probability that a randomly drawn card is either an odd number or a spade is:\n\\[\n\\frac{25}{52} = \\frac{5}{13}\n\\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\\). I hope it is correct."
"First, we need to determine the time it took for the plane to travel 20,000 feet at a speed of 250 miles per hour.\n\nSince 1 mile is equal to 5280 feet, we can convert the distance to miles:\n\\[\n\\frac{20,000 \\text{ feet}}{5280 \\text{ feet per mile}} = \\frac{20,000}{5280} \\text{ miles} = \\frac{50}{13} \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the distance a plane traveling at 400 miles per hour would travel in the same amount of time:\n\\[\n400 \\text{ miles per hour} \\times \\frac{50}{13} \\text{ miles} = 400 \\times \\frac{50}{13} \\text{ feet} = 400 \\times 3.8462 \\text{ feet} \\approx 1534 \\text{ feet}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the plane would travel \\(\\boxed{1534}\\) feet."
