"The circumference of a circle is given by the formula \\( C = 2\\pi r \\), where \\( r \\) is the radius.\n\nFor the first circle with radius 1.125:\n\\[ C_1 = 2\\pi \\times 1.125 = 2\\pi \\]\n\nFor the second circle with diameter 2.25:\n\\[ C_2 = \\pi \\times \\frac{2.25}{2} = \\pi \\times 1.125 \\]\n\nThe ratio of the circumference of the first circle to the circumference of the second circle is:\n\\[ \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{C_1}{C_2} = \\frac{2\\pi}{\\pi \\times 1.125} = \\frac{2}{1.125} = \\frac{2 \\times 8}{1.125 \\times 8} = \\frac{16}{9} \\]\n\nTherefore, the ratio is:\n\\[ \\boxed{16:9} \\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(\\boxed{16:9}\\). I hope it is correct."
