"To simplify \\(\\sqrt{32670}\\), we can factorize the number under the square root into its prime factors.\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorization of 32670:\n\\[\n32670 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 5 \\times 7 \\times 105\n\\]\n\nNext, we factorize 105:\n\\[\n105 = 3^2 \\times 5^2\n\\]\n\nSo, the prime factorization of 32670 is:\n\\[\n32670 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 5 \\times 7 \\times 3^2 \\times 5^2\n\\]\n\nWe can pair the prime factors:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{32670} = \\sqrt{(2 \\times 3)^2 \\times 5 \\times 7} = \\sqrt{6^2 \\times 5 \\times 7} = 6 \\times 5 \\times 7 = 210\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified form is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{210}\n\\]"
"To solve the equation \\(2^3 \\cdot 3^x = 72\\), we start by simplifying the left-hand side. Notice that \\(72\\) can be written as \\(2^3 \\cdot 3^2\\). Therefore, we can rewrite the equation as:\n\n\\[2^3 \\cdot 3^x = 2^3 \\cdot 3^2.\\]\n\nNext, we combine the exponents on the left-hand side:\n\n\\[2^3 \\cdot 3^x = 2^{3+x} \\cdot 3^x = 2^{3+x} \\cdot 3^2.\\]\n\nSince the bases are the same, we can equate the exponents:\n\n\\[3 + x = 2.\\]\n\nSolving for \\(x\\), we get:\n\n\\[x = -2.\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{-2}\\)."
