"To determine the height of the tree, we can use the concept of similar triangles. The woman and her shadow form one triangle, and the tree and its shadow form another triangle. Since the sun's rays are parallel, these triangles are similar.\n\nLet's denote the height of the tree as \\( h \\) feet. The height of the woman is 5 feet, and the length of her shadow is 8 feet. The length of the tree's shadow is 120 feet.\n\nSince the triangles are similar, the ratios of the corresponding sides are equal. Therefore, we can set up the following proportion:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{5}{8} = \\frac{h}{120}\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\( h \\), we can cross-multiply:\n\n\\[\n5 \\times 120 = 8 \\times h\n\\]\n\n\\[\n600 = 8h\n\\]\n\nNext, we divide both sides by 8:\n\n\\[\nh = \\frac{600}{8}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nh = 75\n\\]\n\nThus, the height of the tree is \\(\\boxed{75}\\) feet."
