"To find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 315 and 108, we can use the Euclidean algorithm. The Euclidean algorithm involves repeated division and taking remainders until we reach a remainder of 0.\n\n1. Divide 315 by 108 and find the remainder:\n   \\[\n   315 \\div 108 = 3 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 9\n   \\]\n\n2. Now, divide 108 by 9 and find the remainder:\n   \\[\n   108 \\div 9 = 12 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n   \\]\n\n3. Next, divide 9 by 9 and find the remainder:\n   \\[\n   9 \\div 9 = 1 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n   \\]\n\nSince the remainder is now 0, we stop here. The last non-zero remainder is 9. Therefore, the greatest common divisor of 315 and 108 is 9.\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{9}\\)."
