"To find the largest prime factor of 78, we need to determine its prime factorization.\n\n1. Start by dividing 78 by the smallest prime number, which is 2:\n   \\[\n   78 \\div 2 = 39\n   \\]\n   So, 2 is a factor of 78.\n\n2. Next, divide 39 by the next smallest prime number, which is 3:\n   \\[\n   39 \\div 3 = 13\n   \\]\n   So, 3 is a factor of 78.\n\n3. Now, divide 13 by the next smallest prime number, which is 13:\n   \\[\n   13 \\div 13 = 1\n   \\]\n   So, 13 is a factor of 78.\n\nThe prime factorization of 78 is:\n\\[\n78 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 13\n\\]\n\nThe largest prime factor of 78 is 13. \n\nTherefore, the largest prime factor of 78 is \\(\\boxed{13}\\)."
