"To solve the problem, we need to evaluate the expression \\(\\sqrt{x^2} - 3\\) when \\(x = 6\\).\n\nStep 1: Substitute \\(x = 6\\) into the expression.\n\\[\n\\sqrt{x^2} - 3 \\quad \\text{becomes} \\quad \\sqrt{6^2} - 3\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Calculate \\(6^2\\).\n\\[\n6^2 = 36\n\\]\nSo the expression now is:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{36} - 3\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Take the square root of 36.\n\\[\n\\sqrt{36} = 6\n\\]\nSo the expression now is:\n\\[\n6 - 3\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Perform the subtraction.\n\\[\n6 - 3 = 3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\sqrt{x^2} - 3\\) when \\(x = 6\\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(3\\). I hope it is correct."
