"To solve the problem \\(\\frac{25}{4} \\div \\frac{1}{12}\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Recall that dividing by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying by its reciprocal. The reciprocal of \\(\\frac{1}{12}\\) is \\(\\frac{12}{1}\\).\n\n2. Rewrite the division as a multiplication:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{25}{4} \\div \\frac{1}{12} = \\frac{25}{4} \\times \\frac{12}{1}\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{25 \\times 12}{4 \\times 1} = \\frac{300}{4}\n   \\]\n\n4. Simplify the fraction by dividing the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 4:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{300 \\div 4}{4 \\div 4} = \\frac{75}{1} = 75\n   \\]\n\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{75}\\)."
"To find the value of \\( x \\) given the equations \\( 2x + 3y = 4 \\) and \\( y = 34 \\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute the value of \\( y \\) into the first equation.\n2. Solve for \\( x \\).\n\nFirst, substitute \\( y = 34 \\) into the equation \\( 2x + 3y = 4 \\):\n\n\\[ 2x + 3(34) = 4 \\]\n\nNext, perform the multiplication:\n\n\\[ 2x + 102 = 4 \\]\n\nNow, isolate the term with \\( x \\) by subtracting 102 from both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ 2x = 4 - 102 \\]\n\nSimplify the right-hand side:\n\n\\[ 2x = -98 \\]\n\nFinally, solve for \\( x \\) by dividing both sides by 2:\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{-98}{2} \\]\n\n\\[ x = -49 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{-49}\\)."
