"To determine the number of ways to select 2 balls from a bin of 20 balls where the order does not matter, we use the combination formula:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nHere, \\( n = 20 \\) and \\( k = 2 \\). Plugging in these values, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{20}{2} = \\frac{20!}{2!(20-2)!} = \\frac{20!}{2! \\cdot 18!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by canceling out the common terms in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{20}{2} = \\frac{20 \\times 19 \\times 18!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 18!} = \\frac{20 \\times 19}{2 \\times 1} = \\frac{380}{2} = 190\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of ways to select 2 balls from 20 is \\( \\boxed{190} \\)."
