"The reflection matrix over a vector $\\begin{pmatrix} a \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix}$ is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{R} = \\frac{1}{1 - a^2 - b^2} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -b \\\\ -b & a \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFor the vector $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix}$, we have $a = 1$ and $b = 5$. Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{R} = \\frac{1}{1 - 1^2 - 5^2} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{1}{-24} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe determinant of this matrix is:\n\n\\[\n\\det \\mathbf{R} = \\frac{1}{-24} \\cdot (1(1) - (-5)(-5)) = \\frac{1}{-24} \\cdot (-24) = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]"
