"The dot product of two vectors \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{w}\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w} = \\|\\mathbf{v}\\| \\|\\mathbf{w}\\| \\cos \\theta\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(\\theta\\) is the angle between the vectors. Given that \\(\\|\\mathbf{v}\\| = 3\\) and \\(\\|\\mathbf{w}\\| = 4\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w} = 3 \\cdot 4 \\cdot \\cos \\theta = 12 \\cos \\theta\n\\]\n\nTo find the minimum value of \\(\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w}\\), we need to find the minimum value of \\(12 \\cos \\theta\\). The cosine function \\(\\cos \\theta\\) ranges from \\(-1\\) to \\(1\\). Therefore, the minimum value of \\(\\cos \\theta\\) is \\(-1\\).\n\nThus, the minimum value of \\(12 \\cos \\theta\\) is:\n\n\\[\n12(-1) = -12\n\\]\n\nSo the minimum value of \\(\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w}\\) is \\(\\boxed{-12}\\)."
"We can simplify the right-hand side of the equation using the tangent addition formula:\n\n$$\\tan{19x^{\\circ}}=\\frac{\\cos{96^{\\circ}}+\\sin{96^{\\circ}}}{\\cos{96^{\\circ}}-\\sin{96^{\\circ}}}=\\tan{96^{\\circ}}.$$\n\nSince the tangent function is periodic with period $180^{\\circ}$, we have:\n\n$$\\tan{96^{\\circ}}=\\tan{(96^{\\circ}+180^{\\circ})}=\\tan{276^{\\circ}}.$$\n\nTherefore, the equation becomes:\n\n$$\\tan{19x^{\\circ}}=\\tan{276^{\\circ}}.$$\n\nSince the tangent function is periodic with period $180^{\\circ}$, we have:\n\n$$19x^{\\circ}=276^{\\circ}+180^{\\circ}k,$$\n\nwhere $k$ is an integer. Solving for $x$, we get:\n\n$$x=14+10k.$$\n\nThe smallest positive integer solution is $x=\\boxed{14}$.\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $14$. I hope it is correct."
